payload.message:
Three focused refactoring changes were made:

1. **`ExceptionHelper.java`** — Fixed a stale version string: `"3.x operators and sources"` → `"4.x operators and sources"`. This error message surfaces in user-visible `NullPointerException`s from null-check helpers throughout the library, so it was referencing the wrong major version.

2. **`ObservableCount.java`** — Added a `done` guard flag to `CountObserver.onError()` and `onComplete()`, bringing it in line with every other observer in the codebase (e.g. `AllObserver`, `AnyObserver`, `ReduceObserver`). Without the guard, a misbehaving upstream could cause the downstream to receive duplicate terminal signals (two `onError` calls, or both `onNext(count)+onComplete` and `onError`).

3. **`NotificationLite.java`** — Removed the redundant hand-written `equals()` override from the `ErrorNotification` record. Java records automatically generate `equals()` using `Objects.equals()` on each component, which is identical in behavior to the removed override. The unused `java.util.Objects` import was also cleaned up.

Changes from the last iteration:

```diff
diff --git a/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/operators/observable/ObservableCount.java b/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/operators/observable/ObservableCount.java
index ba6ffb0bb..e133335fd 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/operators/observable/ObservableCount.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/operators/observable/ObservableCount.java
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ package io.reactivex.rxjava4.internal.operators.observable;
 import io.reactivex.rxjava4.core.*;
 import io.reactivex.rxjava4.disposables.Disposable;
 import io.reactivex.rxjava4.internal.disposables.DisposableHelper;
+import io.reactivex.rxjava4.plugins.RxJavaPlugins;

 public final class ObservableCount<T> extends AbstractObservableWithUpstream<T, Long> {
     public ObservableCount(ObservableSource<T> source) {
@@ -32,6 +33,8 @@ public final class ObservableCount<T> extends AbstractObservableWithUpstream<T,

         Disposable upstream;

+        boolean done;
+
         long count;

         CountObserver(Observer<? super Long> downstream) {
@@ -63,11 +66,20 @@ public final class ObservableCount<T> extends AbstractObservableWithUpstream<T,

         @Override
         public void onError(Throwable t) {
+            if (done) {
+                RxJavaPlugins.onError(t);
+                return;
+            }
+            done = true;
             downstream.onError(t);
         }

         @Override
         public void onComplete() {
+            if (done) {
+                return;
+            }
+            done = true;
             downstream.onNext(count);
             downstream.onComplete();
         }
diff --git a/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/util/ExceptionHelper.java b/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/util/ExceptionHelper.java
index 2995df6b8..d2c6d8154 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/util/ExceptionHelper.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/util/ExceptionHelper.java
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@ public final class ExceptionHelper {
      * @since 3.0.0
      */
     public static String nullWarning(String prefix) {
-        return prefix + " Null values are generally not allowed in 3.x operators and sources.";
+        return prefix + " Null values are generally not allowed in 4.x operators and sources.";
     }

     /**
diff --git a/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/util/NotificationLite.java b/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/util/NotificationLite.java
index 0ce9ef495..43cef2cb5 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/util/NotificationLite.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/util/NotificationLite.java
@@ -15,7 +15,6 @@ package io.reactivex.rxjava4.internal.util;

 import java.io.*;

-import java.util.Objects;
 import static java.util.concurrent.Flow.*;

 import io.reactivex.rxjava4.core.Observer;
@@ -40,14 +39,6 @@ public enum NotificationLite {
         public String toString() {
                 return "NotificationLite.Error[" + e + "]";
             }
-
-        @Override
-        public boolean equals(Object obj) {
-            if (obj instanceof ErrorNotification(Throwable e1)) {
-                return Objects.equals(e, e1);
-            }
-            return false;
-        }
